0,Munda languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Munda_languages,"9 hours ago - Sora–Gorum Juang ↔ Kharia ↔ Gutob–Remo ↔ Gtaʔ · Note: ""↔"" = shares certain innovative isoglosses (structural, lexical). In Austronesian and Papuan linguistics, this has been called a ""linkage"" by Malcolm Ross.",Kharia,Austro-Asiatic
1,Kharia people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kharia_people,"May 16, 2026 - The Kharia are an Austroasiatic tribal ethnic group from east-central India. They speak the Kharia language, which belongs to Munda branch of Austroasiatic languages. They are sub-divided into three groups known as the Hill Kharia, Delki Kharia and the Dudh Kharia.",Kharia,Austro-Asiatic
2,Ethnic minorities in Bangladesh - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethnic_minorities_in_Bangladesh,"April 5, 2026 - According to the Ethnologue, there are 36 indigenous living linguistic communities, which include 17 Sino-Tibetan, 10 Indo-European, 7 Austro-Asiatic and 2 Dravidian language-speaking groups.",Kharia,Austro-Asiatic
3,Austroasiatic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austroasiatic_languages,"3 days ago - According to Chaubey et al., ""Austro-Asiatic speakers in India today are derived from dispersal from Southeast Asia, followed by extensive sex-specific admixture with local Indian populations."" According to Riccio et al., the Munda peoples are likely descended from Austroasiatic migrants from ...",Kharia,Austro-Asiatic
4,Kharia language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kharia_language,"March 30, 2026 - The causative derivation increases the valency of a verb stem by introducing a higher or superordinate agent who causes the lower agent to act or a non-agentive event to happen. In Kharia, the signature marker of the Austroasiatic family -(o)(ʔ)b- (including allomorphs) is used as the causative ...",Kharia,Austro-Asiatic
5,Music of Asia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Asia,"May 23, 2026 - Asian music encompasses numerous musical styles, diverse cultural and religious traditions, and forms originating on the Asian continent. ... Wikimedia Commons has media related to Asian music.",Kharia,Austro-Asiatic
6,Kharia,https://www.scstrti.in/index.php/communities/tribes/91-tribes/174-kharia,Cases of theft and homicide are adjudicated in the village council. Thakurani or the Earth Goddess is the supreme deity of the Hill Kharia. They also worship Dharni Devta and a hero named Banda. They have the tradition of dance and music performed on different occasions.,Kharia,Austro-Asiatic
7,"Who are the Kharia Tribe — Tradition, Culture, and History",https://hindusanatanvahini.com/en/who-are-the-kharia-tribe/,"October 19, 2025 - During these festivals, the village resonates with music, dance, and communal feasts. There are no spectators — everyone participates. This collective involvement is the strength of their society. The Kharia language is the heartbeat of their community. It belongs to the Austro-Asiatic family and encompasses a rich world of folklore, songs, and proverbs.",Kharia,Austro-Asiatic
8,Kharia History,http://lisindia.ciil.org/Kharia/Kharia_hist.html,"Kharia, being an indigenous group falls in “Austroliod” group but distinctly resembles Mongoloid. The language spoken by them is also known as ‘Kharia’. The arrival of Kharias belongs to ‘Kolarian tribe’. Their folk songs are fully informative about their past dynamic life.",Kharia,Austro-Asiatic
9,Austro-Asiatic Languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/austro-asiatic-languages/,"July 5, 2010 - Website by David Stampe and Patricia Donegan, University of Hawaii, on the Austro-Asiatic languages where you will find lexicons for Sora, Gorum, Gutob, Remo, Gata, Kharia, Juang, Korku and Santali as well as typologies, bibliographies and maps",Kharia,Austro-Asiatic
